  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 502.10 “Not known to the board (NKTB)” as applied to a path or participant means an individual can seek guidance on, or assistance with finding, treatment for an impai",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 502.10 “Not known to the board (NKTB)” as applied to a path or participant means an individual can seek guidance on, or assistance with finding, treatment for an impairment or potential impairment from an approved provider without the knowledge of the applicable board or any other regulatory authority. The term includes full participation in a program agreement without the knowledge of the applicable board.\n\nSource. #13971, eff 7-1-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc500.html"
